      "side": 1,
      "message": "`boot_to_type` below calls `boot_to`, which does `clear_job_queue()` (badfish.py:1132) before setting the one-time boot. If this `_apply_bootmode` queues a BootMode change, that clear removes the job, and Dell\u0027s guidance is that the pending values have to be set again after a job is deleted, so the reboot applies only the one-time boot. `_ensure_bootmode` normally reconciles the mode earlier, so this is latent, but it means the reconciliation here cannot take effect. Consider clearing before `_apply_bootmode` and calling `send_one_time_boot` without the clear, or dropping this call and relying on `_ensure_bootmode`.",
      "revId": "1d0a6dce5f1d4b78efa5ccc0ea3484d986312e22",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
