      "side": 1,
      "message": "`error_handler` raises on any non-2xx, but Dell returns 400 RAC1035 \"There are no pending values to be cleared\" when there is nothing pending (iDRAC8/9 message registry; the iDRAC8 Redfish guide lists 400/RAC1035 for this action). `_clear_bootmode_jobs` at standard.py:392 aborts the rebuild when this returns False, so a retry after a BMC read error or a failed set with nothing pending now aborts instead of retrying. Return early for RAC1035, or treat it as success.",
      "revId": "1d0a6dce5f1d4b78efa5ccc0ea3484d986312e22",
